1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,660
What happened to the clavichord?
那架古钢琴怎么了？

2
00:00:14,660 --> 00:00:17,510
What happened to the clavichord?
那架古钢琴怎么了？

3
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:23,110
We have an old musical instrument.
我家有件古乐器。

4
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:27,070
It is called a clavichord.
它被叫做古钢琴。

5
00:00:28,370 --> 00:00:31,680
It was made in Germany in 1681.
它是1681年德国制造的。

6
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:36,080
Our clavichord is kept in the living room.
我们的这架古钢琴存放在起居室里。

7
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:40,250
It has belonged to our family for a long time.
我们家有这件乐器已经很久了。

8
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:46,190
The instrument was bought by my grandfather many years ago.
这件乐器是我祖父在很多年以前买的。

9
00:00:47,470 --> 00:00:50,500
Recently it was damaged by a visitor.
可它最近被一个客人弄坏了。

10
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:54,570
She tried to play jazz on it!
因为她用它来弹奏爵士乐！

11
00:00:54,860 --> 00:01:00,830
She struck the keys too hard and two of the strings were broken.
她在击琴键时用力过猛，损坏了两根琴弦。

12
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:04,390
My father was shocked.
我父亲大为吃惊。

13
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:07,850
Now we are not allowed to touch it.
现在不许我们再碰它。

14
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:11,610
It is being repaired by a friend of my father's.
父亲的一个朋友正在修理它。
